  "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{y}}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{R}(\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}})({e}^{y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x]_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}\u20611)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
